          "reason": "K2_C0002 has a substantively interpretable biological identity: a coherent transcriptomic phenotype (oxidative phosphorylation down, immune/inflammatory and proliferative programs) and a coherent ccRCC driver mutation phenotype (VHL and PBRM1 enrichment, BAP1 depletion, VHL surviving global adjustment). Membership representation is consistently positive across all four native geometries (CT 0.069, RNA 0.096, WSI 0.204, WXS 0.275; negative fractions 0.021-0.271), providing affirmative independent representation. The pair boundary is weak but not absent (silhouettes positive in all modalities; within-side affinity 0.645 vs between-side 0.397; ARI 0.744), and the union is single-cluster-dominated (candidate_k=1), which is merge-compatible but not positive evidence for preserving two units; no supported split or merge is available (only split is a permitted structural action, and internal subdivision is single-cluster-dominated with only a modest, imbalanced k=2 candidate). Measured site and CT acquisition factors associate with membership, but these are unadjusted associations without demonstrated persistence after adjustment and do not specifically limit the biological identity; they weigh against terminal acceptance only if they remain a plausible explanation, which is not established here. K2_C0002 remains a defensible independent discovery-stage unit."
