          "reason": "K2_C0001 has interpretable biology (reciprocal transcriptomic phenotype and ccRCC driver mutation pattern with VHL/PBRM1 depletion and BAP1 enrichment), but its exact-set membership is broadly unsupported: native-geometry mean silhouettes are negative in CT (-0.035), WSI (-0.083), and WXS (-0.069) with high negative fractions (0.727, 0.782, 0.473), meaning members are on average closer to the competing set K2_C0002; only RNA is weakly positive (0.063). The relevant pair boundary is weak and conflicting (small positive silhouettes in all modalities but substantial negative fractions in CT 0.437 and WSI 0.456; normalized-cut cost 0.773 reflecting non-trivial cross-boundary connectivity), so affirmative boundary evidence of independence is lacking. No supported structural revision is available: only split is permitted, and internal subdivision is single-cluster-dominated (leading eigengap 0.817 at k=1) with only a modest, non-corroborated k=2 candidate. Measured site and CT acquisition factors remain plausible candidate-specific alternative explanations for membership (tissue_source_site V=0.434 q=0.009; ct_phase, ct_scanner_model, ct_slice_thickness, ct_z_spacing all adjusted-significant) without demonstrated persistence after adjustment. With broadly unsupported membership, weak/conflicting boundaries, no better structural revision, and no remaining decision-relevant evidence that could rescue it, K2_C0001 lacks sufficient defensible discovery value."
